        <body>
            <div xml:id="d502">

                <pb facs="0859" n="789" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg789"/>

                <head>No. 503.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-08-14"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 14,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 57.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your No. 14 of the 12th ultimo, in which
                    you communicate the text of your note of the 2d to the minister of state on the
                    general subject of the claims of our citizens growing out of the embargo of
                    their estates in Cuba during the late insurrection there, is approved. Your Nos.
                    15–23 in separate cases of these claims have been read, and the action which
                    they report is commended.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
